WEBVTT

00:00.990 --> 00:06.930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

00:00.990 --> 00:06.930
Just like the cruel angel

00:06.930 --> 00:14.590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

00:06.930 --> 00:14.590
Young boy, become a legend

00:18.990 --> 00:22.410
2D4U PRESENTS:

00:22.770 --> 00:25.810
Aoi kaze ga ima

00:22.770 --> 00:25.810
Even though the untested breeze...

00:25.810 --> 00:29.510
mune no doa o tataitemo

00:25.810 --> 00:29.510
...taps at the door to your heart

00:29.510 --> 00:36.970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

00:29.510 --> 00:36.970
You just look solely at me and smile

00:37.560 --> 00:44.500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

00:37.560 --> 00:44.500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

00:44.500 --> 00:51.400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

00:44.500 --> 00:51.400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

00:52.000 --> 00:55.750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

00:52.000 --> 00:55.750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

00:55.750 --> 00:58.340
sono senaka ni wa

00:55.750 --> 00:58.340
...that upon your back

00:59.510 --> 01:02.960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

00:59.510 --> 01:02.960
You have the wings with which to fly...

01:02.960 --> 01:06.310
no hane ga aru koto

01:02.960 --> 01:06.310
...towards the distant future

01:06.990 --> 01:10.690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

01:06.990 --> 01:10.690
The cruel angel's thesis

01:10.690 --> 01:14.430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

01:10.690 --> 01:14.430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

01:14.430 --> 01:18.200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

01:14.430 --> 01:18.200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

01:18.200 --> 01:21.900
Omoide o uragiru nara

01:18.200 --> 01:21.900
If you are to betray our memories

01:21.900 --> 01:25.540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

01:21.900 --> 01:25.540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

01:25.540 --> 01:29.270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

01:25.540 --> 01:29.270
Young boy, become a legend

01:51.670 --> 01:55.010
Is he going to skip school again?

01:55.970 --> 01:57.970
Little Shin's Room

01:58.890 --> 02:02.810
Shinji, wake up! How long are you going
to keep skipping school?

02:02.810 --> 02:06.310
It's been five days now. Unit 01 has
already been completely repaired.

02:06.310 --> 02:09.150
So don't you think the pilot needs
to get his act together too?

02:09.150 --> 02:10.440
Shinji?!

02:19.740 --> 02:21.910
Miss Misato Katsuragi

02:27.870 --> 02:30.670
He's run away.
I suppose that's not surprising.

02:30.710 --> 02:35.170
EPISODE 04
RAIN, AFTER RUNNING AWAY

02:42.470 --> 02:43.550
Shinji?

02:44.390 --> 02:46.020
Well...

02:48.430 --> 02:52.110
We're Ikari's classmates,
Aida and Suzuhara, Ma'am.

02:52.110 --> 02:54.020
Aida and Suzuhara?

02:54.020 --> 02:54.690
Yes, Ma'am!

02:54.690 --> 02:56.730
I'm Suzuhara.

02:57.650 --> 03:00.570
Aren't you the boys who got in
Unit 01's entry plug?

03:00.570 --> 03:01.200
Yes, Ma'am!

03:01.200 --> 03:03.700
We're sorry for causing so much trouble.

03:04.530 --> 03:08.250
Actually, Ikari's been absent ever since then,

03:08.250 --> 03:10.710
so we came to see if he was okay.

03:10.710 --> 03:14.420
He's at the Nerv training facility right now.

03:14.420 --> 03:16.090
Oh, I see.

03:16.090 --> 03:19.800
These are the printouts that were
building up on Ikari's desk.

03:19.800 --> 03:22.390
Oh, sorry for your trouble. Thank you.

03:22.390 --> 03:24.600
Well, we'll be leaving now.

03:24.600 --> 03:26.930
Please say "hi" to Ikari for us.

03:26.930 --> 03:29.730
Yeah, I will. Bye.

03:35.730 --> 03:38.320
This is an unexpected development.

03:38.320 --> 03:40.450
She was a real babe, wasn't she?

03:43.870 --> 03:45.580
Shinji, you idiot!

03:49.750 --> 03:51.000
Idiot!

03:56.750 --> 04:00.380
<i><i>The next station is
Nagao Toge, Nagao Toge.</i></i>

04:00.380 --> 04:02.930
<i><i>The exit will switch to the right side.</i></i>

05:00.020 --> 05:08.370
<i><i>Thank you for using New Tokyo-3
Loop Seven.</i></i>

05:08.370 --> 05:11.740
<i><i>This train will be going out of service
at this station.</i></i>

05:12.160 --> 05:16.170
<i><i>Please, make sure you take all of your
belongings as you exit the train.</i></i>

05:21.960 --> 05:23.340
I've got to go back.

05:24.340 --> 05:26.930
<i>Hey there! We're offering you
a great bargain!</i>

05:26.930 --> 05:29.140
<i>Hot young babes serving
heavenly refreshment!</i>

05:29.140 --> 05:32.970
<i>Special services to heal your tired body,
services to fill you with energy!</i>

05:35.100 --> 05:36.850
<i>You really couldn't detect it, Doctor?!!</i>

05:36.850 --> 05:39.520
<i>Yes. An object only ten
millimeters in diameter</i>

05:39.520 --> 05:43.070
<i>crashed into Antarctica at close
to the speed of light.</i>

05:43.070 --> 05:46.450
<i>The technology we had was unable
to predict or prevent such a thing.</i>

05:46.450 --> 05:49.240
<i>It's like hell out there! Just what is
the purpose of science?!</i>

05:50.120 --> 05:53.200
<i>The atmospheric flux caused by the
change in the Earth's axis</i>

05:53.200 --> 05:55.160
<i>has decreased by 3%.</i>

05:55.160 --> 05:57.330
<i>So it's getting a little better?</i>

05:57.330 --> 06:00.750
<i>No, there's still a tidal wave approaching
at 230 meters a second!</i>

06:00.750 --> 06:02.380
<i>Doctor! We must evacuate!</i>

06:02.380 --> 06:05.090
<i>It's my duty to remain here.</i>

06:05.090 --> 06:07.090
<i>Doctor, choosing death is easy,</i>

06:07.090 --> 06:10.050
<i>but you have an obligation
to watch this living hell!</i>

06:16.930 --> 06:25.900
Documentary!
The World Sinks...
Second Impact
Tokyo-2
Tokyo

07:22.880 --> 07:23.750
Idiot.

07:27.670 --> 07:30.630
Arrival Stop Only

08:16.680 --> 08:18.760
He's only fourteen years old.

08:19.720 --> 08:23.480
It seems so cruel, making him bear
the burden of mankind's destiny.

08:23.850 --> 08:29.820
But we have no choice but to entrust the
piloting of the Evas to fourteen year olds.

08:30.070 --> 08:31.530
I know.

08:31.530 --> 08:34.070
So, has he called?

08:35.530 --> 08:36.740
No?

08:39.200 --> 08:42.910
No. I think he might never come back.

08:43.620 --> 08:45.370
What are you going to do?

08:45.370 --> 08:47.000
Nothing really.

08:47.000 --> 08:49.300
If he won't come back,
maybe that's for the better.

08:50.000 --> 08:50.800
Why?

08:51.710 --> 08:54.340
After the battle the other day...

08:55.840 --> 08:58.350
Why did you ignore my order?

08:59.260 --> 09:00.720
I'm sorry.

09:01.140 --> 09:04.060
I'm the one who's in charge
of your operations, right?

09:04.060 --> 09:04.770
Yes.

09:04.770 --> 09:08.900
You have a duty to obey my orders.
Do you understand?

09:08.900 --> 09:09.820
Yes.

09:09.820 --> 09:11.900
I'm warning you, never do it again.

09:11.900 --> 09:12.570
Yes.

09:12.570 --> 09:15.070
Do you really understand what I'm saying?!

09:15.070 --> 09:16.110
Yes.

09:16.110 --> 09:20.830
Hey, you're not going to get out of this
by just saying yes to everything I say.

09:20.830 --> 09:25.250
I know that. That's enough, isn't it?
We won the battle anyway.

09:26.370 --> 09:30.340
You know, it may seem easy to go along
with whatever anyone else wants,

09:30.340 --> 09:33.260
but if you get into the Eva with that attitude,
it'll kill you!

09:33.260 --> 09:35.670
I don't care.

09:36.260 --> 09:38.970
It'd be nice if I could say you've got
the right attitude,

09:38.970 --> 09:42.600
but if you expect to get any praise out of me,
you're wrong, Shinji Ikari.

09:42.600 --> 09:46.690
That's not the point. In any case, I'm the
only one who can pilot it, aren't I?

09:48.020 --> 09:49.360
I'll do it.

09:49.940 --> 09:51.480
I see.

09:54.240 --> 09:58.360
If piloting an Eva means nothing
but pain to him,

09:58.360 --> 10:00.030
he shouldn't get into it again.

10:01.240 --> 10:02.790
Otherwise, I'm sure he'll get killed.

10:02.790 --> 10:04.870
But we need pilots.

10:12.380 --> 10:14.090
Captain!

10:15.260 --> 10:16.800
Aida, go on ahead!

10:17.420 --> 10:21.930
But I can't go and leave you behind!

10:22.720 --> 10:23.970
You fool!

10:34.150 --> 10:35.860
Upsy-daisy.

10:41.120 --> 10:42.410
The new kid?

10:43.280 --> 10:44.160
Ikari!

11:00.550 --> 11:02.970
Summer Training Drill Operation Outline
Today's Scheduled Operations
15:00 Deploy for Combat
16:00 Prepare for Attack,
Commence Firing

11:01.680 --> 11:05.060
Toji was sorry about that.

11:05.060 --> 11:07.770
He said that his kid sister scolded him

11:07.770 --> 11:11.350
and said that, "It was the robot
who saved our lives!"

11:11.770 --> 11:15.730
That's pretty embarrassing, being
chewed out by a grade school kid.

11:16.230 --> 11:17.030
Right?

11:21.490 --> 11:25.490
I like it at night because those
noisy cicadas don't chirp.

11:26.120 --> 11:28.410
Although I remember that it was pretty quiet
when I was a kid,

11:28.410 --> 11:30.580
there've been more of them each year.

11:30.580 --> 11:33.040
The ecosystem is returning
to its former state.

11:33.040 --> 11:34.290
That's what Miss Misato said.

11:35.790 --> 11:37.550
I see, Miss Misato said so.

11:37.550 --> 11:39.420
I really envy you.

11:39.420 --> 11:43.840
Living with such a beautiful woman
and piloting the Evangelion.

11:43.840 --> 11:48.850
I wish I could get behind
the controls just once!

11:49.310 --> 11:52.770
You shouldn't. I think your mother
would be worried.

11:54.270 --> 11:57.940
Oh, don't worry about that. I don't have one.

12:00.030 --> 12:01.530
I'm the same as you.

12:04.110 --> 12:06.280
You'll have something to eat, won't you?

12:06.280 --> 12:07.370
Yeah.

12:08.450 --> 12:10.500
Do you usually do this sort of thing?

12:10.500 --> 12:13.250
Huh? Well, sure.

12:13.540 --> 12:17.090
Is this some kind of training for
guerilla warfare or something?

12:17.090 --> 12:21.010
How could I fight with toys like these?
It's just for fun.

12:45.950 --> 12:48.620
You're Shinji Ikari, aren't you?

12:48.620 --> 12:49.790
Yes.

12:49.790 --> 12:52.410
We're from Nerv Security Intelligence.

12:52.410 --> 12:57.210
Under Article 8 of the Security Act,
we're taking you to headquarters.

12:57.580 --> 12:58.960
All right?

12:58.960 --> 12:59.420
Yes.

13:03.380 --> 13:06.760
And all you did was stand there?

13:07.090 --> 13:08.510
That's easy for you to say!

13:08.510 --> 13:11.720
But it's like I said, they were Nerv
Security Intelligence, professionals.

13:11.720 --> 13:16.440
So what?! Don't you have any balls at all?!

13:16.440 --> 13:17.190
Sissy!

13:17.190 --> 13:17.900
Pervert!

13:17.900 --> 13:18.520
Ape!

13:18.520 --> 13:21.280
Only an idiot fights when
he knows he can't win.

13:21.280 --> 13:22.900
Balls have nothing to do with it.

13:34.660 --> 13:36.460
Long time, no see.

13:36.460 --> 13:37.420
Yes.

13:37.420 --> 13:40.840
Do you feel any better after wandering
around for two days?

13:41.380 --> 13:42.760
I don't know.

13:43.090 --> 13:46.090
The Eva is on standby. Will you pilot it?

13:47.130 --> 13:48.510
Or won't you?

13:49.300 --> 13:52.510
You're not going to scold me
for running away?

13:55.680 --> 13:59.100
Of course not. I'm not related to you, am I?

14:00.560 --> 14:04.530
If I say that I won't pilot Unit 01,
what will you do with it?

14:05.240 --> 14:06.990
I suppose that Rei will do it.

14:08.200 --> 14:09.450
Won't you pilot it?

14:10.280 --> 14:15.410
It seems unrealistic for you
to force everything on her.

14:15.410 --> 14:18.120
Don't worry. I'll pilot it.

14:18.120 --> 14:19.830
But you don't want to do it?

14:19.830 --> 14:23.960
Of course not. To begin with, it's not
something that comes to me naturally.

14:24.340 --> 14:27.380
But Ayanami, Miss Misato and Miss Ritsuko...

14:27.380 --> 14:29.220
Cut that out!

14:29.220 --> 14:31.300
This has nothing to do with any of us!

14:31.300 --> 14:33.260
If you don't like it, get out of here!

14:33.260 --> 14:37.310
Just forget all about Eva and us and
go back to where you came from!

14:38.850 --> 14:42.270
We don't need someone
with that attitude piloting!

14:53.240 --> 14:57.290
The Third Child is leaving
New Tokyo-3 tomorrow.

14:57.290 --> 15:00.250
Then we'll reconfigure
Unit 01's system for Rei.

15:00.250 --> 15:01.500
But...

15:01.500 --> 15:04.670
Regardless of the results of Unit 00's
re-activation experiments,

15:04.670 --> 15:06.920
we'll move on to experimenting with Unit 01.

15:12.050 --> 15:14.640
According to the Marduk
Organization's report,

15:14.640 --> 15:17.470
the Fourth Child hasn't been found yet.

15:17.470 --> 15:20.350
That means we can't get
any pilot replacements?

15:23.230 --> 15:27.730
Excuse me, where is Miss Misato?
I'd like to say goodbye.

15:27.730 --> 15:30.650
You're no longer Nerv personnel.

15:30.650 --> 15:33.120
Therefore, we can't give you any information.

15:46.750 --> 15:47.880
Ikari!

15:47.880 --> 15:49.050
You forgot this!

15:58.930 --> 16:01.520
Could you excuse me for a moment?

16:04.610 --> 16:07.110
Thank you.

16:09.070 --> 16:10.400
Hey, Toji.

16:10.400 --> 16:11.950
Come on, say something!

16:14.450 --> 16:19.370
Ikari, I'm sorry I hit you twice.
Please, hit me back!

16:19.370 --> 16:21.000
I can't do that.

16:21.000 --> 16:23.710
Please! Otherwise, I won't be satisfied.

16:23.710 --> 16:26.080
See? He's a pretty embarrassing guy,
isn't he?

16:26.080 --> 16:28.460
But if it'll put an end to this dispute,
why don't you go ahead and hit him?

16:30.050 --> 16:31.010
But...

16:31.010 --> 16:33.630
Hurry up! You don't have
much time, do you?

16:34.010 --> 16:36.550
Okay, but only once.

16:36.550 --> 16:38.220
Okay! Come on!

16:42.270 --> 16:43.600
Hold it!

16:45.520 --> 16:47.190
No holdin' back.

16:47.190 --> 16:48.230
Right.

16:51.070 --> 16:51.860
Ouch...

17:03.410 --> 17:04.750
How did you know I'd be here?

17:04.750 --> 17:10.210
Call it a hunch. We've seen
dozens of classmates off now.

17:12.840 --> 17:18.430
If you're leavin', we'll have to leave
this city sometime soon,

17:18.430 --> 17:25.480
but we can't blame you for that.
We saw how you suffered in the Eva.

17:25.850 --> 17:28.810
And if anyone tries to blame you,

17:29.650 --> 17:31.280
I'm gonna give them a head butt!

17:35.200 --> 17:37.990
Hey, don't look so gloomy.

17:37.990 --> 17:39.320
Take care.

17:39.320 --> 17:40.490
Good luck!

17:40.490 --> 17:41.580
Well...

17:42.870 --> 17:44.200
It's time.

18:12.230 --> 18:14.530
I'm the one who deserves to be hit!

18:14.990 --> 18:18.660
I'm a scoundrel, a coward,

18:19.820 --> 18:22.910
spineless and weak...

18:24.120 --> 18:26.290
Don't give us any more trouble.

18:33.250 --> 18:39.010
<i>Eva Unit 01 will be entering Stage 2
cryo-stasis for activation system rewrite.</i>

18:39.010 --> 18:40.140
He's gone.

18:43.890 --> 18:45.600
Was it for the best?

18:46.060 --> 18:48.270
The "Hedgehog's Dilemma".

18:49.310 --> 18:52.400
The closer we become,
the more deeply we hurt each other.

18:53.070 --> 18:54.900
Now I understand.

18:56.990 --> 18:58.400
That boy...

18:59.450 --> 19:03.660
He can't let others know how he feels
in any other way.

19:04.830 --> 19:09.750
<i>The Express Linear Train bound
for Atsugi is arriving on Track 2.</i>

19:09.750 --> 19:13.840
<i>For your safety, please step back
to the area inside the yellow lines.</i>

19:15.460 --> 19:18.050
<i>The train arriving on Track 2 is for
special government use only</i>

19:18.050 --> 19:21.180
<i>and departs at 4:20 for Atsugi.</i>

19:21.180 --> 19:24.430
<i>No civilians are allowed inside the fence.</i>

19:24.430 --> 19:26.350
<i>Please be aware that the
boarding of this train</i>

19:26.350 --> 19:29.890
<i>by unauthorized persons
is strictly prohibited.</i>

19:41.280 --> 19:42.660
Hang in there.

20:17.320 --> 20:18.570
Look!

20:18.570 --> 20:20.990
It's that babe!

21:14.540 --> 21:18.880
<i>The local train bound for Gora
is now arriving on Track 4.</i>

21:19.250 --> 21:23.470
<i>For your own safety, please stay
inside the yellow lines.</i>

21:24.010 --> 21:26.180
<i>If you're accompanying small children,</i>

21:26.180 --> 21:28.090
<i>please ensure that they are
properly supervised.</i>

21:29.510 --> 21:35.440
<i>The train arriving on Track 4 is the
local shuttle to Gora departing at 4:32.</i>

21:35.810 --> 21:39.520
<i>If this is your train, please step inside
and wait until departure.</i>

21:40.230 --> 21:45.400
<i>The train is now approaching.
Please stay behind the yellow line.</i>

21:49.410 --> 21:51.580
I... I'm home.

21:56.000 --> 21:57.580
Welcome home.

21:57.620 --> 22:00.590
TO BE CONTINUED

23:06.070 --> 23:07.030
PREVIEW

23:06.820 --> 23:10.660
Rei Ayanami limits her association
with others as much as possible.

23:10.660 --> 23:13.870
The only one she opens up to
is Commander lkari.

23:13.870 --> 23:17.160
Shinji is at a loss to understand this girl,
who is closer to his own father than he is.

23:17.160 --> 23:20.170
Next Evangelion: "Rei, Beyond the Heart"

23:18.410 --> 23:21.080
REI, BEYOND THE HEART
